ing that was  booked this dimension is the output of a  machine learning model so itself it  takes a long time to compute and it  lands later in the day so if we waited  for this dimension and all the other  dimensions  that we needed to show up in order to  land bookings data every day that would  be a big problem for a company because  every team in the company would have to  wait until like after work hours in  order to understand the number of  bookings that happened yesterday so to  solve this we introduced a concept  called dimension sets and these  dimension sets give our data scientists  control over their own assaleh z-- for  their their section of that metric r and  the dimensions associated with it so  instead of just specifying a list of  dimensions in our config we now have a  dimension set section the China team can  define their own dimensions shown here  in purple ish and the host team can  define their set of dimensions shown  here in yellow and we automatically  create two different tables one table  for each dimension set and the metrics  are in both of those tables and if a new  team needs to be able to cut their  metric by a different set of dimensions  they can just add new dimension a new  dimension set to this config just a  couple lines of not even code a couple  lines of Yahoo config and will  automatically create another table for  them and load this table and to Druid so  that it's there for super fast slice and  dice analytics so we've actually started  to think about our metrics framework as  a de normalization machine this is where  this is why it has become so powerful in  order to be able to make quick decisions  and understand what's what's happening  in our business because now every team  is empowered to cut I to be able to look  at the metrics they care about cut by  whatever dimensions they want they can  produce these tables in by just writing  a couple of lines in a config and within  a day the data is there populated  backfil